                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h2 class="accordion-header">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq2">
                            How is data scoped between Sales Executives and Managers?
                        </button>
                    </h2>
                    <div id="faq2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            Row-level security is enforced via <code>ICurrentUserService</code>. Sales Executives only see customers, leads, opportunities, and follow-ups assigned to their user ID. Sales Managers see team-wide pipelines and reports, while Administrators have unrestricted system control.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h2 class="accordion-header">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq3">
                            Does the platform provide RESTful API endpoints?
                        </button>
                    </h2>
                    <div id="faq3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            Yes. The platform provides full JSON REST API endpoints under <code>/api/customers</code>, <code>/api/leads</code>, <code>/api/opportunities</code>, <code>/api/followups</code>, and <code>/api/reports</code>, using dedicated DTOs and standard HTTP status codes.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h2 class="accordion-header">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faq4">
                            How does the audit trail safeguard against parameter collisions?
                        </button>
                    </h2>
                    <div id="faq4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            The audit log subsystem uses explicit query binding (<code>actionFilter</code>) to eliminate collisions with ASP.NET Core's default MVC route action token, ensuring search filters and query expressions execute reliably across all criteria.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

